#!/bin/bash
# clang for the XNU build on Linux (after HackiOS's xnu-clang): an Apple Mach-O target (macOS 14.0,
# as Xcode 15 builds this kernel), flags only Apple's clang knows dropped, ld64 of the cctools.
HB="$(cd "$(dirname "$(readlink -f "$0")")" && pwd)"   # (also when called as /usr/bin/xcrun)
# (C++: no __cxa_atexit for exceptions-style cleanup; global destructors: see cc_kext/cc_kext_stubs.c)
case "$(basename "$0")" in *++) drv=clang++; extra=(-fno-use-cxa-atexit);; *) drv=clang; extra=();; esac
args=()
for a in "$@"; do
  case "$a" in
    -enable-trivial-auto-var-init-zero-knowing-it-will-be-removed-from-clang) ;;
    -fapple-kext-vtable-verify|-Wno-vla-cxx-extension) ;;
    -Werror|-Werror=*|-Weverything|-pedantic-errors) ;;
    -Wl,-new_linker) ;;                    # Xcode 15's ld-prime; ld64 of the cctools is the classic one
    -lcc_kext) args+=("${XNU_CC_KEXT:-/work/fakeroot/usr/local/lib/kernel/libcc_kext.a}");;   # stock clang drops it (no Darwin runtimes)
    *) args+=("$a");;
  esac
done
# -mcpu=generic: for an arm64-apple-macos target stock clang otherwise assumes an Apple M1 and, next to
# the kernel's -march=armv8.2-a, emitted ARMv8.3/8.4 instructions (xpaci, ldapur, stlur) the
# Pixel's Cortex-A76/A55 do not have: the first one hung the boot after SWEET EARLY 5.
exec /usr/bin/$drv -include /opt/host/inc/xnu_clang_compat.h -target arm64-apple-macos14.0 -mcpu=generic --ld-path="$HB/ld64" \
  -w "${extra[@]}" "${args[@]}"
